                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s35IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>بِسمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيْمِ قَدْ سَمِعَ اللهُ قَوْلَ الَّتِي تُجَادِلُكَ فِى زَوْجِهَا وَتَشْتَكِى اِلَى اللهِ</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#14v">-14v</locus>وَصَدَّقَتْ بِكَلِمَاتِ رَبِّهَا وَكُتُبِهِ وَكَانَتْ مِنَ القَانِتِيْنَ</explicit>
                     <note>58:1-66:12. The manuscript was repaired, and two bifolios were installed on the top of the bloc of quires to replace the text which was missing.  The last folio of the manuscript was taken away later on. Thirteen to fourteen lines a page. Titles of suras rubricated. Words left uncompleted at the end of the line are rewritten in full on the following line. Catchwords. In the margins, mark of ḥizb, red color (9r), few corrections, and a clarification (tawḍīḥ, 11r). The identification of the scribe is based on notes in ASH00276 (fol. 13r) and ASH00265 (fol. 1r).</note>
                     <note/>
